    "https://www.usherbrooke.ca/recherche/en/udes/career-opportunities": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "Career Opportunities - Research - Université de Sherbrooke Aller au contenu Pour une expérience de navigation optimale, veuillez activer Javascript sur votre navigateur. Université de Sherbrooke Logo de l'Université de Sherbrooke Découvrir L' UdeS Programmes et admission La Recherche Partenariats Communauté étudiante Personnel de L' UdeS Outils Changer l'avenir Emplois monPortail Bottin Demande d’aide informatique (Casius) Dictionnaire Usito Genote Impression mobile (SIMUS) Microsoft 365 Moodle Tous les services informatiques monPortail Mon dossier étudiant Mon emploi Mon dossier de bibliothèque Mon accès Mon profil UdeS Courriel USherbrooke Tout le site Web Bottin Programmes Université de Sherbrooke Logo de l'Université de Sherbrooke Changer l'avenir Courriel USherbrooke monPortail Mon dossier étudiant Mon emploi Mon dossier de bibliothèque Mon accès Mon profil UdeS Demande d’aide informatique (Casius) Impression mobile (SIMUS) Genote Microsoft 365 Moodle Tous les services informatiques Changer l'avenir Emplois monPortail Bottin Découvrir l' UdeS Programmes et admission La Recherche Partenariats Communauté étudiante Personnel de L' UdeS Research English en Français fr Home Research at the UdeS Unifying Themes Our Unique Identity World-Class Lecture Series Renowned Expertise Clusters of Research Excellence Support We Provide Career Opportunities Studying in research Why Choose The UdeS? Preparing An Admission Application We are recruiting researchers Governance Office of the Vice-President, Research Affiliated Institutions Responsibilities Policies and directives Research Council Contact the Vice-President's Office Menu Home Research at the UdeS Unifying Themes Our Unique Identity Our Unique Approach Research Partnerships Research Intensity University-Industry Collaborations Partnered Chairs Digital Health Incomparable Environment A Campus Dedicated to Health Campus in Montérégie Parc Innovation-ACELP Facilities Fostering Creativity Unique Infrastructures Carrefour d'innovation en technologies écologiques (CITE) Centre for Scientific Computing (CCS) MiQro Innovation Collaborative Centre (C2MI) Scale-up Centre Centre des technologies avancées (CTA) BRP-UdeS Multiscale Research Complex in Hydrology, Hydraulics, and Environment Performance, Hydration and Thermoregulation Laboratory Integrated Research Laboratory for the Development of Materials and Sustainable and Innovative Structures Solar Park - Canada's largest! SIRENE Station Research Platforms World-Class Lecture Series Renowned Expertise Major Distinctions Tremplin Award Tremplin Award - 2023 Recipients Tremplin Award - 2022 Recipients Tremplin Award - 2021 Recipients Research and Creation Award Discovery of the Year by Québec Science Clusters of Research Excellence Research Centres Research Chairs Eddie Goldenberg Research Chairs of Canada Canada Excellence Research Chairs Canada Research Chairs Granting Agencies Chairs Institutional Chairs Research Institutes Centre de recherche Charles-Le Moyne (CRCLM) Research Centre on Aging (CdRV) Pharmacology Institute of Sherbrooke (IPS) Université de Sherbrooke Cancer Research Institute (IRCUS) Interdisciplinary Institute for Technological Innovation (3IT) Institut quantique (IQ) Institut universitaire de première ligne en santé et services sociaux (IUPLSSS) International Clusters International Research Center CNRS International Research Laboratories (IRL) Pôle universitaire de santé numérique de l’Estrie Support We Provide Finding Funding Creating a Research Platform Enhancing the Value of Intellectual Property Mentoring Program Supervising Research Students Career Opportunities Studying in research Why Choose The UdeS? Personalized Support Mentoring Committee Scholarships Programs The most generous research excellence scholarships Additional Sources of Financial Assistance Support for Scholarships Applications Promoting Student Research Research Presentation Scholarships Competitions Leading to Work Dissemination Research and Graduate Studies Celebration Support for Student Research Activities Drafting Days Assistance for Holding Scientific Symposiums Assistance with Creating Scientific Posters Development of Complementary Skills Undergraduate Introductory Research Internships Postdoctoral Fellowships Centre CR+ Entrepreneurship and Social Innovation Fast-Track Programs Interdisciplinarity and Networking Preparing An Admission Application Define Your Subject Preparing An Application File Concluding a Mentoring Agreement Support for Finding a Research Director Reference Table We are recruiting researchers Research Projects Governance Office of the Vice-President, Research Our Core Values Strategic Objectives Inclusive and Welcoming Environment Affiliated Institutions Responsibilities Responsible Conduct of Research Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Policies and directives Research Council Contact the Vice-President's Office You are here Research Research at the UdeS Career Opportunities Career Opportunities The Université de Sherbrooke is inviting applications for professor positions. Université de Sherbrooke is: One of the most prolific research university in Canada. A bold combination of entrepreneurial culture, pooled infrastructure and interdisciplinary vision. Cutting-edge facilities and specialized resources contributing to productive research and propelling research careers. From fundamental research to practical applications, we bring together expertise from across the board, working with broad international networks to develop innovative solutions that address major challenges, both current and future. Current Call for Proposals Canada Impact+ Emerging Leaders Program Professor in Engineering Université de Sherbrooke is proud to participate in the 2026 competition of the Canada Impact+ Emerging Leaders Program. As part of this call for applications, the Université de Sherbrooke is seeking new candidates from the international scientific community to recruit a new professor. This is a tenure-track position in the Faculty of Engineering . This position aligns with the strategic priority area of Environment, Climate Resilience and the Arctic . Only candidates who, as of July 5, 2026, are internationally based (working and residing outside Canada) are eligible. Deadline for submitting applications: Wednesday, August 5, 2026 at 5 p.m. Learn more and apply About Canada Impact+ Emerging Leaders Program Canada Impact+ Emerging Leaders is a $120 million investment to help institutions bring more internationally based early career researchers (ECRs) to Canada. The Canada Impact+ Research Chairs program and the Canada Impact+ Emerging Leaders program are related. However, the ECR nominees are expected to have an independent program of research, with potential for impact through collaborations with, but not limited to, the Impact+ Research Chairs. Canada Research Chairs Program Professor - Tier 1 Canada Research Chair Designated group: Indigenous Peoples Participating faculties: Faculty of Science and Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences As part of the call for proposals for the Canada Research Chairs Program (CRCP), the Université de Sherbrooke is seeking applications from individuals who identify as Indigenous to fill a professorship for a Tier 1 CRC. This call for proposals is aimed at both current UdeS professors and external candidates. Deadline for submitting applications: Monday, August 10, 2026 at 5 p.m. [Visual from the work Transmission: de l’importance de bien apprendre à voler by Abenaki-Wendat artist Christine Sioui-Wawanoloath] Learn more and apply Professor - Tier 2 Canada Research Chair Designated group: Persons with disabilities Participating faculties: Faculty of Engineering, Faculty of Science and Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences As part of the call for proposals for the Canada Research Chairs Program (CRCP), the Université de Sherbrooke (UdeS) is seeking applications from the designated group of persons with disabilities to fill a professorship for a Tier 2 Canada Research Chair. This call for proposals is open only to external candidates, meaning individuals who do not currently hold a professorial position at UdeS at the deadline for the current posting. Deadline for submitting applications: Monday, August 10, 2026 at 5 p.m. Learn more and apply Professor - Tier 2 Canada Research Chair Participating faculties: Faculty of Engineering, Faculty of Science and Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences As part of the call for proposals for the Canada Research Chairs Program (CRCP), the Université de Sherbrooke (UdeS) is seeking applications to fill a professorship for a Tier 2 Canada Research Chair. This call for proposals is open only to external candidates, meaning individuals who do not currently hold a professorial position at UdeS at the deadline for the current posting. Deadline for submitting applications: Monday, August 10, 2026 at 5 p.m. Learn more and apply About Canada Research Chairs Program The Canada Research Chairs Program is a prestigious program at the centre of a national strategy to make Canada one of the world's top countries in research and development. Tier 1 Chairs, tenable for seven years and renewable once, are for outstanding researchers acknowledged by their peers as world leaders in their fields. Tier 2 Chairs, tenable for five years and renewable once, are for exceptional emerging researchers, acknowledged by their peers as having the potential to lead in their field. The intent of Tier 2 Chairs is to provide emerging researchers with support that will kick-start their careers. About Université de Sherbrooke A Key Player in Research Université de Sherbrooke is a nationally and internationally renowned Canadian institution. Research at Université de Sherbrooke is booming at an unprecedented rate, and this great vitality is evidenced by our prestigious ranking among Canada’s Top 50 Research Universities. Our university has the highest increase in its research activities in Canada over the last 10 years, ranking among the 10 universities with the highest research revenues in the country in 2023. Université de Sherbrooke is one of the country’s leading research universities. Our unique approach to research Our approach to university research is premised on a bold combination of entrepreneurial culture , pooled infrastructure and professional expertise , and interdisciplinary vision . This has led to our ranking among the most prolific research universities in Canada. An open, engaged, responsible, and inclusive community The primary value that motivates the Université de Sherbrooke is giving individuals special attention, in particular through the development of a study and work environment conducive to each person’s growth. Furthermore, the university places great importance on both respecting diversity and promoting the outreach potential of each member of its community. At a Glance: Research at Université de Sherbrooke Research revenues totalling $245,7M in 2024-2025 A research community of over 6,600 people 6 niches of excellence, encouraging interdisciplinary research 7 research institutes 18 research centres 105 research chairs, including 2 Canada Excellence Research Chairs 2 CNRS international research laboratories: Nanotechnologies & Nanosystems and Quantum Frontiers 1 CNRS international research centre: Innovation for a sustainable planet An institutional network of research platforms offering highly specialized pooled services and equipment Partner in the Pôle universitaire de santé numérique de l'Estrie An incomparable environment that trains the next generation of scientists Over 100 research excellence scholarships awarded each year A support structure designed to facilitate technology transfer More information about Université de Sherbrooke and its incomparable environment About Université de Sherbrooke Research at the Université de Sherbrooke Equity, diversity and inclusion at Université de Sherbrooke (French) An exceptional working and living environment (French) Liens généraux Contacter l'UdeS Plans des lieux et accès routiers Emplois Santé et sécurité Sécurité de l'information Urgence Découvrir l'UdeS Programmes et admission Recherche Communauté étudiante Personnel de l’UdeS International Formation continue UTA FACULTÉS, CENTRES ET INSTITUTS Droit École de gestion Éducation Génie Lettres et sciences humaines Médecine et sciences de la santé Sciences Sciences de l'activité physique Centres et instituts SERVICES Bibliothèques, archives et gestion de l'information Centre culturel Centre sportif La Fondation Ressources financières Ressources humaines Stages et développement professionnel Tous les services MÉDIAS Relations médias Actualités et événements Répertoire des médias sociaux CAMPUS PRINCIPAL : 2500, boul. de l'Université, Sherbrooke (Québec) J1K 2R1, 819 821‑8000 CAMPUS DE LA SANTÉ : 3001, 12 e Avenue Nord, Sherbrooke (Québec) J1H 5N4, 819 821‑8000 CAMPUS DE LONGUEUIL : 150, place Charles‑Le Moyne, C. P. 200, Longueuil (Québec) J4K 0A8, 1 888 463‑1835 (sans frais), 450 463‑1835 , Site Web Tous droits réservés © Université de Sherbrooke Accessibilité Conditions d'utilisation Politique de confidentialité Paramètres des témoins Ce site Web utilise des fichiers témoins (cookies) essentiels à son bon fonctionnement.\n                    Vous pouvez paramétrer l'utilisation de témoins facultatifs nous permettant d'optimiser votre expérience à travers le site. Voir la Politique de confidentialité Gérer les paramètres Autoriser les témoins Paramètres des témoins Pour obtenir plus d’information sur la nature et l’utilisation des témoins, voir la Politique de confidentialité . Témoins essentiels Ces témoins sont nécessaires au bon fonctionnement du site Web. Ils permettent de maintenir\n                        l’accès à certaines sections sécurisées et de conserver des critères de recherche, par exemple.\n                        Ces témoins ne peuvent être désactivés. Toujours autorisés Témoins analytiques Ces témoins nous aident à comprendre votre utilisation de notre site Web et nous permettent d'améliorer l’expérience qu'il propose. Autoriser Témoins publicitaires Ces témoins sont utilisés pour vous proposer des publicités pertinentes en fonction de votre navigation sur notre site. Ces publicités peuvent être émises par l'Université de Sherbrooke ou d'autres entités. Autoriser Annuler Enregistrer"
